 "Hay restos de un poblado vikingo en Terranova, hacia el año 1000.": "There are remains of a Viking settlement in Newfoundland, from around the year 1000.",
 "Eran sucios y desaliñados.": "They were dirty and scruffy.",
 "Se peinaban a diario y el sábado era el «día del baño».": "They combed their hair daily and Saturday was “bath day”.",
 "Las mujeres podían divorciarse.": "Women could get divorced.",
 "Y tener tierras y negocios propios.": "And own land and businesses.",
 "Un clic: se dibuja la ruta y el barco la recorre de Noruega a Terranova; las fechas aparecen a su paso. Navegaban mirando el sol, las estrellas, las aves y el color del agua.": "One click: the route is drawn and the ship sails it from Norway to Newfoundland; the dates appear as it passes. They navigated by the sun, the stars, the birds and the colour of the water.",
